   "html_text": "Any of various free modal or tense logics can be formalized by adding to a language ⟦M⟧ of the sort defined in Section 1.3 the sentential operator ‘ ⟦M⟧ ’. If ⟦M⟧ is a formula, so is ⟦M⟧ . In alethic modal logic, this operator is read “it is necessarily the case that.” More generally, it means “it is true in all accessible worlds that,” where accessibility from a given world is a different relation for different modalities: possibility for alethic logics, permissibility for deontic logics, vario",
